@startuml context-transformation
!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho

title Context Transformation Flow

participant "GUI Editor" as GUI
participant "EditingContext" as Editing
participant "ContextTransformer" as Transformer
participant "GridTransformer" as GridTrans
participant "SimulationContext" as Simulation
participant "jDisco Engine" as jDisco

== Phase 1: Railway Network Editing ==

GUI -> Editing: createEmptyContext()
activate Editing
Editing -> Editing: Initialize grid (Array2DMap<Cell>)
Editing -> Editing: Initialize graph (ExtendedUnorientedGraph)
GUI <-- Editing: EditingContext
deactivate Editing

GUI -> Editing: putCell(point, RailSwitch)
activate Editing
Editing -> Editing: Add NodeCell to grid
Editing -> Editing: Update reverse table
GUI <-- Editing: Success
deactivate Editing

GUI -> Editing: joinCells(from, to, TrackBlock)
activate Editing
Editing -> Editing: Create TrackBlockPart cells
Editing -> Editing: Update graph edges
Editing -> Editing: Record line keys
GUI <-- Editing: Success
deactivate Editing

note over GUI, Editing
    **Editing Phase:**
    - Mutable railway network
    - Static NodeCell objects (RailSwitch, RailSemaphore, InOut)
    - TrackBlockPart for intermediate segments
    - Graph structure for pathfinding
end note

== Phase 2: Transformation to Simulation ==

GUI -> Transformer: createSimulationContext(editingContext)
activate Transformer

Transformer -> Transformer: Validate network completeness
note right: Check all paths connected,\nsemaphores configured, etc.

Transformer -> GridTrans: transformGrid(editingContext.grid)
activate GridTrans

GridTrans -> GridTrans: Create new Array2DMap<Cell>
loop for each cell in editing grid
    alt cell is NodeCell (RailSwitch/RailSemaphore/InOut)
        GridTrans -> GridTrans: Create DynamicPathSeparator wrapper
        note right
            Static → Dynamic mapping:
            - RailSwitch → DynamicRailSwitch
            - RailSemaphore → DynamicRailSemaphore
            - InOut → DynamicInOut
        end note
    else cell is TrackBlockPart
        GridTrans -> GridTrans: Copy TrackBlockPart unchanged
    end
    GridTrans -> GridTrans: Put in new grid at same Point
end

Transformer <-- GridTrans: Transformed grid with dynamic wrappers
deactivate GridTrans

Transformer -> Transformer: Create DefaultSimulationContext
Transformer -> Transformer: Copy graph structure
Transformer -> Transformer: Transfer track blocks and InOuts
Transformer -> Transformer: Initialize dynamic maps

Transformer -> Simulation: new DefaultSimulationContext(cols, rows, factory)
activate Simulation
Simulation -> Simulation: Set cells (transformed grid)
Simulation -> Simulation: Set graph (copied)
Simulation -> Simulation: Initialize dynamicMap, trackMap
Transformer <-- Simulation: SimulationContext instance
deactivate Simulation

GUI <-- Transformer: SimulationContext
deactivate Transformer

note over Transformer, Simulation
    **Transformation Guarantees:**
    - One-way: Editing → Simulation (no reverse)
    - Immutable network after transformation
    - Static objects wrapped by dynamic wrappers
    - Identity preserved (wrapper.equals(static))
    - Grid structure and Point mappings preserved
end note

== Phase 3: Simulation Execution ==

GUI -> Simulation: run()
activate Simulation

Simulation -> Simulation: processFactory.createMainProcess(this)
note right: Factory creates Generator or custom LoopProcess

Simulation -> Simulation: processFactory.createInOutWorker(this, inOut)
note right: Factory creates InOutWorker for each InOut

Simulation -> jDisco: Activate main process
activate jDisco
note right: jDisco discrete event simulation begins

Simulation -> Simulation: toDynamic(RailSwitch) → DynamicRailSwitch
note right: Lazy wrapper creation and caching

jDisco -> Simulation: Get/set dynamic state (semaphore signals, switch conf)
Simulation -> Simulation: Update DynamicPathSeparator wrappers

note over Simulation, jDisco
    **Simulation Phase:**
    - Immutable railway network structure
    - Mutable dynamic state (signals, switches, trains)
    - Dynamic wrappers manage state
    - jDisco manages time and events
end note

... Simulation runs until endTime ...

GUI -> Simulation: stop()
Simulation -> jDisco: Deactivate processes
jDisco --> Simulation: Stopped
deactivate jDisco

Simulation -> Simulation: Report statistics
GUI <-- Simulation: Simulation results
deactivate Simulation

== Post-Simulation ==

note over GUI, Simulation
    **After Simulation:**
    - SimulationContext is discarded
    - To run again, transform from editing context again
    - No way to convert simulation back to editing
    - Editing context remains unchanged and reusable
end note

@enduml
